# Deploy CloudStore Django App to Render

Your project is a Django 4.2 app with MySQL, AWS S3, and email. Render offers free PostgreSQL but **not free MySQL**, so we'll switch the database to **PostgreSQL** on Render (Render's free tier includes a PostgreSQL instance). Your file storage stays on AWS S3 and all other secrets stay in environment variables.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Migration: MySQL → PostgreSQL**
> Render's free tier only provides PostgreSQL, not MySQL. We will switch the database backend to PostgreSQL for the deployed version. Your local dev can still use MySQL. The migration is straightforward since Django abstracts the DB layer — no model changes needed, just a new DB driver (`psycopg2-binary`) and updated settings.

> [!WARNING]
> **Your `.env` file contains real secrets** (AWS keys, DB password, email app password). We will NOT commit `.env` to Git. All secrets are set via Render's environment variable dashboard.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Your current AWS credentials are visible in `.env`**. Since this file is in your project folder, ensure `.env` is in your `.gitignore` before pushing to GitHub. We will create/verify `.gitignore` as a first step.

