## Proposed Changes

### 1. Git & Security Setup

#### [NEW] `.gitignore`
- Ensure `.env`, `venv/`, `__pycache__`, `*.pyc`, `staticfiles/`, `media/`, `ngrok.exe` are excluded from Git

---

### 2. Configuration Files for Render

#### [MODIFY] `requirements.txt`
- Add `psycopg2-binary` (PostgreSQL driver)
- Add `gunicorn` (production WSGI server)
- Add `dj-database-url` (parse DATABASE_URL from Render's environment)

#### [NEW] `build.sh`
- Shell script Render runs on deploy:
  ```bash
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
  python manage.py migrate
  ```

#### [NEW] `render.yaml`
- Render blueprint file defining the web service and environment variables

---

### 3. Django Settings Updates

#### [MODIFY] `cloudstore/settings.py`
- Use `dj-database-url` to auto-parse `DATABASE_URL` (Render injects this for PostgreSQL)
- Set `DEBUG=False` in production (read from env)
- Add Render's domain to `ALLOWED_HOSTS` and `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`
- Keep whitenoise for static files (already installed ✅)

---

## Deployment Steps (Post-Approval)

1. Create `.gitignore` and verify secrets are excluded
2. Update `requirements.txt` with PostgreSQL + gunicorn
3. Create `build.sh` and `render.yaml`
4. Update `settings.py` for production database
5. Initialize a local Git repo and push to GitHub
6. Connect GitHub repo to Render
7. Set all environment variables in Render dashboard

---

## Render Environment Variables to Set

| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
| `SECRET_KEY` | A new secure random key |
| `DEBUG` | `False` |
| `ALLOWED_HOSTS` | `your-app.onrender.com` |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Auto-set by Render PostgreSQL |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | Your AWS key |
| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | Your AWS secret |
| `AWS_STORAGE_BUCKET_NAME` | `shubham-cloudstore-mca` |
| `AWS_S3_REGION_NAME` | `ap-south-1` |
| `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | Your encryption key |
| `EMAIL_BACKEND` | `django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend` |
| `EMAIL_HOST` | `smtp.gmail.com` |
| `EMAIL_PORT` | `587` |
| `EMAIL_USE_TLS` | `True` |
| `EMAIL_HOST_USER` | Your Gmail |
| `EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD` | Your Gmail app password |
| `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` | Your Gmail |

